# Agent guide

**Orcan** = Docker **context orchestrator** for Cursor CLI (`agent`) and Claude Code (`claude`): workspaces, path-parity mounts, ignore/instruction seeds, browser terminal. Agent CLIs are tools inside it; **models are out of scope**.

Display name: **Orcan**. Technical ids: `orcan`, `ORCAN_*`. **Orcan** is the only product name in docs and user-facing text.

Read root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and [`docs/en/ai/project-context.md`](../../docs/en/ai/project-context.md). This rule is always applied.

## Product ritual (host)

```bash
orcan context wizard  # or init / context add / hand-edit orcan.config.json
orcan sync            # ALWAYS after config changes (up does not call sync)
orcan build           # after Dockerfile / docker/rootfs / tmux / shell changes
orcan up              # daily start (ttyd); orcan up --with-docker for DinD
```

Recreate after sync: `orcan down && orcan up`.

## Config = JSON only

- User profile: **`orcan.config.json`** under `ORCAN_HOME` (default `~/.config/orcan/`).
- Example: `orcan.config.example.json`.
- Keep Compose/docs YAML (`docker-compose*.yml`, `mkdocs.yml`, generated `mounts/*.yml`).
- Do not revive YAML user configs.

## Runtime stack (container)

```text
ttyd (cursor-ttyd) → agent-launcher → tmux 3.6a → zsh
  Starship · autosuggestions · syntax-highlighting · fzf
  aliases: /etc/orcan/shell/aliases.sh
  lazygit + delta (git UI)
```

| Concern | Source of truth |
| --- | --- |
| Terminal UI map | `docs/en/guides/terminal-ui.md` (+ PL); rule `.cursor/rules/terminal-ui.mdc` |
| ttyd theme | `docker/rootfs/usr/local/bin/cursor-ttyd` (`dark`/`navy`, `mocha`) |
| tmux | `docker/rootfs/etc/tmux/` + `Dockerfile` `TMUX_VERSION` (3.6a static) |
| zsh | `docker/rootfs/etc/skel/.zshrc` + `.zshrc.d/` |
| starship / lazygit / git seeds | `docker/rootfs/opt/orcan/` (**missing-only** into `~/.config` / `~/.gitconfig`) |
| Cursor defaults | `docker/rootfs/opt/cursor-defaults/` → seeded missing-only |

When changing colours or shell chrome: keep the navy/cyan palette aligned across layers; no TPM / Oh My Zsh / Nerd Font requirement. After rootfs/Dockerfile edits: `orcan build` then recreate.

